<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96802" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στικτός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στίζω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>pricked, tattooed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βραχίονες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.10
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γράμματα ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Le.</u>
				19.28
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>spotted, dappled</i>, of fallow-deer, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				184
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>El.</u>
				568
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεβρίδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					111
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				835
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλαφος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.1293c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕαιναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>C.</u>
					3.288
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βασιλεὺς . . ς. οἷον ταὧς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>Im.</u>
					2.31
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. πτέρυξ</span>, of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔποψ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				304.8
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στικτοῖς ὄμμασιν
			δεδορκότα</span>, i.e. with eyes all over the body, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1115
			</span></i>.</div>
